# Git & Delivery — {{PROJECT_NAME}}

The stories behind each rule: `.claude/knowledgebase/lessons/git.md` (add one when a rule is born).

## Identity & remotes
- Commit as {{GIT_IDENTITY}} (set per repo when it differs from global); remote {{REMOTE}}. Branch, commit, push and PR inside the repo you changed.

## Flow
- Sync before you start, before you believe a gate, and before you push: `git fetch origin`, read `git log --oneline HEAD..origin/{{BASE_BRANCH}}`, merge it in. Gate the MERGED tree.
- Branch from `{{BASE_BRANCH}}` (`feat/<short-name>`, `fix/<short>`); never commit to `{{DEFAULT_BRANCH}}` directly; continue a matching remote branch if one exists.
- Commit per logical slice with a clear message, ending `Co-Authored-By: <the model that made the commit> <noreply@anthropic.com>`.
- **Push ONCE, when the feature is ready and its gate green** (every push runs the pre-push hooks and usually a preview deploy). The one extra push is a backup when a session ends with commits only local.
- Open the PR into `{{BASE_BRANCH}}` and merge it yourself (`gh pr merge --merge --match-head-commit <sha>`) once the gate is green on the head merged with `{{BASE_BRANCH}}`; then deploy the non-production environments. No review step by default: the AI review cycle (`pr-review-cycle`) runs only when the developer asks. **A merge or release to production waits for the developer's go.**
- Never force-push a shared branch; never `--no-verify`; never commit secrets (git-ignored and hook-blocked).

## One worktree per agent
- Parallel agents each get their own git worktree (the plugin's `worktree.sh new <feature>`), removed when done. A read-only agent (reviewer, researcher, QA) never runs `git stash`, `reset`, `checkout`, `switch`, `restore`, `clean` or a commit.

## The index
- Commit with a pathspec (`git commit -m "…" -- <paths>`), never `git add -A` blind; read `git diff --cached --name-only` first; check `git show --stat HEAD` after; never rewrite a pushed commit.

## Before committing / pushing
- Run the gate ({{GATE}}), a clean build, a real check of the change, and the KB update in the same change.
